<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Generalizability to Qwen-2.5-7B</h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ C.4 Generalizability to Qwen-2.5-7B ‣ Appendix Appendix C Additional Experimental Results ‣ Layer-Targeted Multilingual Knowledge Erasure in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> presents the CKA-LRDS analysis for Qwen-2.5-7B, which identifies Layer 19 as the target layer. Table <a href="#A3.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ C.4 Generalizability to Qwen-2.5-7B ‣ Appendix Appendix C Additional Experimental Results ‣ Layer-Targeted Multilingual Knowledge Erasure in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> presents the corresponding unlearning results. At Layer 2 (shallow), we observe catastrophic forgetting in the Retain Set, with German accuracy dropping from 13.0% to 3.0%. Unlearning fails at Layer 23 (deep), as Forget accuracy remains high (English: 45.0% vs. finetuned 52.0%). At Layer 19 (target), the method achieves optimal erasure (26.0%) while preserving utility across languages.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F3" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.22562v1/dual_metric_qwen.svg" id="A3.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:333/196;" width="333" height="196"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F3.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 3</span>: </span><span id="A3.F3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;">Identifying the language-agnostic region for Qwen-2.5-7B.<span id="A3.F3.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> Blue line: multilingual CKA alignment (higher is better). Red line: LRDS (lower is more language-agnostic). Green shaded area: </span>language-agnostic region<span id="A3.F3.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> <math id="A3.F3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, satisfying both <math id="A3.F3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{CKA}&gt;\tau_{\text{align}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>CKA</mtext><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>align</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{CKA}&gt;\tau_{\text{align}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.F3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{LRDS}&lt;\tau_{\text{spec}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>LRDS</mtext><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>spec</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{LRDS}&lt;\tau_{\text{spec}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where thresholds are computed via Equation <a href="#S4.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ 4.1 Identifying Language Agnostic Region ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ Layer-Targeted Multilingual Knowledge Erasure in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. We select Layer 19 as the optimal intervention point.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.T10" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A3.T10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 10</span>: </span><span id="A3.T10.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Qwen-2.5-7B (RMU) across Layers.<span id="A3.T10.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Layer 19 represents the target layer. Shallow intervention (L2) causes Retain collapse in held-out languages, while deep intervention (L23) fails to erase knowledge. The target layer (L19) achieves optimal balance between erasure and utility preservation. Asterisks (*) denote source languages (<math id="A3.T10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{src}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>src</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{src}}</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></span></figcaption>
<div id="A3.T10.6" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:226.1pt;vertical-align:-111.4pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-85.7pt,56.1pt) scale(0.668216939391859,0.668216939391859) ;">
<table id="A3.T10.6.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A3.T10.6.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T10.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="A3.T10.6.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Language</span></th>
<th id="A3.T10.6.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T10.6.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Base</span></th>
<th id="A3.T10.6.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T10.6.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Finetuned</span></th>
<th id="A3.T10.6.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" colspan="5"><span id="A3.T10.6.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Unlearned Accuracy by Intervention Layer</span></th></tr>
<tr id="A3.T10.6.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T10.6.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column">(Pre-trained)</th>
<th id="A3.T10.6.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r">(Target)</th>
<th id="A3.T10.6.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column">L2 (Shallow)</th>
<th id="A3.T10.6.1.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column">L12</th>
<th id="A3.T10.6.1.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column">L15</th>
<th id="A3.T10.6.1.2.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column"><span id="A3.T10.6.1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">L19 (Target)</span></th>
<th id="A3.T10.6.1.2.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column">L23 (Deep)</th></tr>
<tr id="A3.T10.6.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T10.6.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" colspan="8"><span id="A3.T10.6.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">FORGET SET: High School Chemistry<span id="A3.T10.6.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (Lower is Better <math id="A3.T10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;" mathbackground="#F2F2F2" stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
